      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense about the bevel angle. I'll try adjusting it to 22 degrees and see if that helps with the slicing action. \n\nOne more thing—I noticed the splintering seems much worse in certain sections of the plank, almost as if the density changed abruptly or the fibers became much more brittle in patches. Could this be related to the seasonal growth rings or perhaps localized variations in moisture retention within the cellular structure? I'm trying to understand if there's a specific pattern to how these \"stubborn\" sections are behaving.",
